    "dateLine": "1:30 p.m. Friday, October 2, 2026, Update",
    "excerpt": "Due primarily to very mild nights, September 2026 concluded as the 13th-warmest on record at Millersville University since 1914. Frequent storm systems and bouts of heavier showers and storms caused monthly rainfall to be about 1.5\" above normal (see below). Despite a cool final third of the month, October kicked off on a much warmer and summery note. …",
